# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is GITIGNORED and must stay that way.
#
# ⚠️ THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. The rendezvous endpoint is an infrastructure
# identifier, which is the entire reason payloads are encrypted — so it must
# never reach a commit. `just check` refuses to run if .env is tracked or
# staged, and `just publish` refuses to push if it is. Those guards are the net;
# this comment is the reason.

# ── Identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The signing key is THE CONTROL CREDENTIAL. It lives outside this repo and is
# only ever read, never copied here.
SIGNING_KEY=$HOME/csramsh-secrets/signing/config_signing_ed25519
NODE_ID=76e99358
# Recipient cert. Defaults to recipients/$NODE_ID.crt if left empty.
RECIPIENT=

# ── The PRIMARY backhaul route ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ A NAME, NEVER A LITERAL. On an IPv6-only carrier an IPv4 literal is
# unroutable — DNS64 synthesises only for names. Must be a DNS-only record,
# not CDN-proxied (proxies carry HTTP/S, not SSH).
#
# ⚠️ LEAVE THESE EMPTY IN THIS FILE. It is COMMITTED, to a PUBLIC repo. The
# real endpoint belongs in .env, which is gitignored. The guards refuse a
# tracked or staged .env — they CANNOT catch a real hostname typed into this
# template, and one was very nearly committed here on 2026-08-18.
BACKHAUL_HOST=
BACKHAUL_USER=
# The rendezvous SSH port — often non-standard.
BACKHAUL_PORT=22
BACKHAUL_BIND=127.0.0.1:2222

# ── Additional routes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Space-separated instance names, each [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*, max 16 chars.
# For a route named `b`, set BACKHAUL_B_HOST / _USER / _PORT / _BIND below.
#
# ⚠️ Two routes are only two routes if the rendezvous genuinely DIFFER. Two
# instances on one host give redundancy against a dead ssh process and nothing
# against a dead network — and on the same host they need different binds.
BACKHAUL_ROUTES=

BACKHAUL_B_HOST=
BACKHAUL_B_USER=
BACKHAUL_B_PORT=22
BACKHAUL_B_BIND=127.0.0.1:2223
